# Telegram bot token from @BotFather
Bot_Token="123456:ABC-DEF..."

# Optional for PDF files over 20 MB: install the official local Telegram Bot API
# with scripts/setup-telegram-local.sh. The installer sets these automatically.
# TELEGRAM_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8082
# TELEGRAM_LOCAL_FILES_DIR=/var/lib/asc-telegram-api

# Optional private web workspace on asc.alamornetwork.ir, installed by setup-web.sh.
# The installer generates WEB_PASSWORD and writes WEB_ORIGIN automatically.
# WEB_PASSWORD=
# WEB_ORIGIN=https://asc.alamornetwork.ir
# WEB_PORT=3000
# WEB_PRINCIPAL_ID=    # only needed when no Telegram owner id is stored

# Optional page rendering after the built-in crawler fails or returns little text.
# Disabled by default. Each crawl batch makes at most two fallback calls.
# Scrapling launches Chromium locally; install it separately with setup-scrapling.sh.
# The browser may open the public host of a search result. Add any extra CDN
# hosts needed to render it; all other cross-site requests are blocked.
# WEB_FETCH_FALLBACK=scrapling,firecrawl
# SCRAPLING_PYTHON=/opt/asc-scrapling/bin/python
# SCRAPLING_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Firecrawl is a hosted, credit-consuming fallback; set only if you want to use it.
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# Optional scholarly discovery. Basic OpenAlex requests also work without a key;
# a free key raises the daily request budget. Never put it in a chat message.
# OPENALEX_API_KEY=

# Optional read-only MCP checks for software-idea reports only.
# GitHub: use a token limited to public repository reads; ASC enables only
# search_code and get_file_contents. Never paste the token into chat.
# GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN=
# Context7: public endpoint can be used without a key; the key raises limits.
# CONTEXT7_MCP_ENABLED=1
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# Optional: Google Document AI batch OCR for large scanned PDFs (up to 500 pages).
# Requires a separate Google Cloud project with billing; Google AI Pro is not sufficient.
# Create an Enterprise Document OCR processor, a bucket in the same region, and a
# service account with Document AI API User + Storage Object Admin on that bucket.
# Keep the JSON key outside this repository and readable only by the web service.
# GOOGLE_DOCUMENT_AI_PROJECT=your-project-id
# GOOGLE_DOCUMENT_AI_LOCATION=us
# GOOGLE_DOCUMENT_AI_PROCESSOR=processor-id
# GOOGLE_DOCUMENT_AI_BUCKET=your-private-bucket
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/etc/asc/google-document-ai.json

# Only this chat id may use the bot. Leave blank on first run — the first chat to
# message the bot claims it, and the id is printed so you can pin it here.
OWNER_CHAT_ID=

# Model provider: the 9router installed on the same server by setup-server.sh.
# Generate this key in the 9router dashboard. It is NOT the MixRoute upstream key.
ROUTER_KEY=""
ROUTER_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:20128/v1"

# Model ids, as that endpoint names them. A gateway usually prefixes the provider
# (liara/google/gemini-3.7-flash); a direct provider usually does not
# (google/gemini-3.7-flash). List what yours accepts:
#   curl -s "$ROUTER_BASE_URL/models" -H "Authorization: Bearer $ROUTER_KEY"
#
# What follows is what measuring actually produced, on liara with a kira free tier
# alongside. The numbers are from one Persian voice note and one research question, so
# treat them as a starting point and re-run the probes on your own material.

# Voice and scanned pages. Must accept audio AND images. A chain because gemini-3.7-flash
# answered 402 on a working key — that model was not in the plan, and without a fallback
# a document simply failed to be read.
#   1,993 toman for 109s of audio, punctuation intact, kept "دیالوگ مکی" correctly
#   3.5-flash-lite is 3.3x cheaper but drops punctuation and erodes proper nouns
#   3.1-flash-lite reads cleanly but turned "دیالوگ مکی" into "دیالوگ‌نویسی" — the
#   failure that matters for research, since it silently replaces a citation
# Check which ones your key may call:  node scripts/probe-vision.js
MODEL_CAPTURE=google/gemini-3.6-flash,google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite,xiaomi/mimo-v2.5

# Web research. This is the one role where cheap models were measured to be worse than
# useless: they invent citations. Per verified claim on the same question —
#   openai/gpt-5.4-mini:online  12,139 toman, 4 of 7 verified, nothing fabricated
#   perplexity/sonar-pro        12,131 toman, 3 of 6 verified
#   perplexity/sonar             2,470 toman, 1 of 8 verified, 6 bad quotes
#   qwen3.7-flash:online           220 toman, 0 verified, invented URLs outright
#   gemini-3.5-flash-lite:online 1,106 toman, 0 verified, cited a Google search page
# Cheap is not cheap here. Re-run it yourself:  node scripts/probe-research.js
MODEL_RESEARCH=openai/gpt-5.4-mini:online,perplexity/sonar-pro

# The highest-volume role — planning and assessing, dozens of calls per investigation —
# so it is where free models pay off most. Every kira free model is listed on purpose:
# which of them is up flips between runs minutes apart, a down link costs one instant
# 502, and the client rests a failed model for two minutes. Ordered by which returned
# valid JSON, since that is all this role ever asks for.
# Ends on something dependable: a free tier runs out mid-investigation.
MODEL_STRUCTURE=qwen3.8-flash-free@kira,glm-5.3-flash-free@kira,qwen3.8-27b-free@kira,kira-auto@kira,kira-mini-1.0@kira,mimo-v2.5-free@kira,hy3-free@kira,glm-5.3-free@kira,ling-3.0-flash-sante-free@kira,mercury-2.5-free@kira,google/gemini-3.6-flash
# Optional reasoning model for full document analysis. Defaults to MODEL_STRUCTURE.
# MODEL_ANALYSIS=deepseek-v4-pro@mixdirect,glm-5.3@mixdirect

# One small classification per message, with the user waiting for it. Its budget is
# patience, not money: the only free model that both answered correctly and came back
# under four seconds was qwen3.8-flash-free at 3.3s.
MODEL_ROUTER=qwen3.8-flash-free@kira,google/gemini-3.6-flash

# Optional, and the biggest cost lever on voice. A multimodal model charges for audio
# as input tokens; a dedicated speech-to-text model charges by length of audio and is
# far cheaper. Set this and a voice note is transcribed here and structured by
# MODEL_STRUCTURE — two cheap calls instead of one expensive one. Leave empty to keep
# the one-call path. Compare them on your own voice first:
#   node scripts/probe-voice.js voice.ogg
MODEL_TRANSCRIBE=

# Retrieval. Neither has an equivalent on a chat-only provider, so these stay where the
# embeddings and the reranker actually live. MODEL_RERANK empty disables reranking;
# retrieval still works, just less precisely.
MODEL_EMBED=intfloat/multilingual-e5-large
MODEL_RERANK=cohere/rerank-v3.5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- more providers
#
# No one endpoint has everything. Declare another with a BASE_URL and its keys, then
# send a role to it by writing `model@name`:
#
#   KIRA_BASE_URL=https://kiraai.vn/api/v1
#   KIRA_KEYS=key-one,key-two,key-three
#   MODEL_STRUCTURE=qwen3.8-flash-free@kira,glm-5.3-free@kira,google/gemini-3.6-flash
#   MODEL_ROUTER=qwen3.8-flash-free@kira,google/gemini-3.6-flash
#
# Quote the whole value or none of it — "a,b,c" and a,b,c both work, "a","b" does not.
#
# Several keys are tried in turn: a key that hits its rate limit rests a minute, one
# that is out of credit half an hour, one that is rejected a day.
#
# The chain is comma-separated and tried left to right. Always end it with something
# you can rely on — a free tier runs out mid-investigation, and with nothing behind it
# the run stops there. See what your own keys can actually reach:
#
#   node scripts/probe-provider.js kira
